A column's type changed with its data: kronor as integers become a price
written out as text. A STRICT column keeps its type, so the ledger makes a
new column, fills it, drops the old one and gives the new one its name.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price INTEGER NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 95), (2, 40);

== after
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, price TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;

== ledger
ALTER TABLE dish ADD COLUMN price_text TEXT;
UPDATE dish SET price_text = CAST(price AS TEXT) || ' kr';
ALTER TABLE dish DROP COLUMN price;
ALTER TABLE dish RENAME COLUMN price_text TO price;

== plan
